[
    {
        "content": "<p>I find it difficult to work with the current <code>Representation.ind</code> <code>Representation.IndV</code>. The current definition of the underlying module of the induced representation is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coinvariants</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Representation</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tprod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">leftRegular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and the elementory generator is defined via</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Coinvariants</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘ₗ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">single</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In practice, <code>simp</code> would unfold them and expose the implementations, so it is really painful to play with them for me... Are these designed in such a way in purpose? I tried to make it a <code>def</code> but it turns out that almost all relevant later implementations would all have to be modified. Probably making them <code>def</code>'s is not the correct thing to do. </p>\n<p>My proposal is that without modifying the current defitions in Mathlib, we should at least record the generator-relation lemmas just as how we mathematically do in paper. More precisely, I think the following lemmas (proofs in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41808\">#41808</a>) should be helpful</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induction_on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk_map_inv_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind_map_conj_mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I want to know if these are reasonable API, or they are redundant because I missed some fundamental intention in the orignal design?</p>",
        "id": 610999446,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784186219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"699016\">@Edison Xie</span></p>",
        "id": 610999897,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784186343
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you don't like some definitions in mathlib, you could always open a refactor PR!</p>",
        "id": 611004102,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1784187748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also I think maybe ind is worth being a def, but I'm opening a refactor of <code>Representation</code> soon, so the refactor of ind should probly happen after that</p>",
        "id": 611004363,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1784187815
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wow, what is wrong with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Representation#doc\">docs#Representation</a> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"699016\">@Edison Xie</span> ?</p>",
        "id": 611126998,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1784223271
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Abbrev.27s.20in.20Representation.2EInduced/near/611126998\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wow, what is wrong with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Representation#doc\">docs#Representation</a> <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"699016\">Edison Xie</span> ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>So when I was doing <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41054\">#41054</a>, I realised that when we're doing restrictions, the way it works now is that we literally compose a <code>G</code>-representation <code>ρ</code> with a homomorphism from <code>H</code> to <code>G</code> to get an <code>H</code>-rep, this is bad because first we're abusing defEq between <code>Representation</code> and <code>MonoidHom</code>, secondly the type we'll be seeing is <code>Rep.of (ρ.comp f)</code> and this is also bad because then we need to abuse defEq between things like <code>Rep.of ((ρ.comp e.symm).comp e))</code> and <code>Rep.of ρ</code> hence I suggest that we change <code>Rep</code> from an abbrev to a one-field structure of monoid homs (I think also this is generically good to seal stuff in the concrete land and then make category stuff as tranparent as possible).</p>",
        "id": 611137049,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1784225731
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>With the new lean version, a plain def will probably be enough to seal things off.</p>",
        "id": 611138417,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1784226159
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"308899\">Yakov Pechersky</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Abbrev.27s.20in.20Representation.2EInduced/near/611138417\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>With the new lean version, a plain def will probably be enough to seal things off.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I know that <code>def</code>s are semi-reducible, but what reducibility is the structure projection nowadays?</p>",
        "id": 611138601,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1784226221
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Please add a def (or abbrev) of <code>Representation.res</code>! At the first time trying to use restriction, I looked up the documentations carefully for a long time and used <code>(Rep.res s (Rep.of ρ)).ρ</code>.</p>",
        "id": 611139885,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784226670
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That will probably lead to typeclass pain later on</p>",
        "id": 611172739,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1784239348
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"699016\">Edison Xie</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Abbrev's.20in.20Representation.2EInduced/near/611137049\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the way it works now is that we literally compose a <code>G</code>-representation <code>ρ</code> with a homomorphism from <code>H</code> to <code>G</code> to get an <code>H</code>-rep, this is bad because first we're abusing defEq between <code>Representation</code> and <code>MonoidHom</code>, </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This isn't abuse if the two are reducible defeq (which currently they are)</p>",
        "id": 611213262,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1784266215
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>I suggest that we change <code>Rep</code> from an abbrev to a one-field structure of monoid homs</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Rep#doc\">docs#Rep</a> is already a structure of more than one field!</p>",
        "id": 611213390,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1784266293
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Abbrev.27s.20in.20Representation.2EInduced/near/611213390\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I suggest that we change <code>Rep</code> from an abbrev to a one-field structure of monoid homs</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Rep#doc\">docs#Rep</a> is already a structure of more than one field!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think he means <code>Representation</code></p>",
        "id": 611213672,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784266448
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"699016\">Edison Xie</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Abbrev.27s.20in.20Representation.2EInduced/near/611004363\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also I think maybe ind is worth being a def</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I am back to this. I tried several times to make <code>IndV.mk</code> a <code>def</code>, but unfortunately it always ended up with adding endless new lemmas. One reason for why it was so unpleasant is that the definition involves </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coinvariants</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ker</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, I found it pretty much managable to work with my Hecke file by adding a <code>def</code> layer upon <code>IndV.mk</code> and disabling the global 'simp' lemma <code>ind_apply</code> (<code>ind</code> is already a <code>def</code> it is the <code>@[simps]</code> on it problematic)! Now at least in my Hecke <code>simp</code> will not unfold the ugly <code>ind</code> anymore and <code>IndV.mk</code> will not even be exposed. Probably I will not try to make <code>IndV.mk</code> a <code>def</code> again <span aria-label=\"face vomiting\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f92e\" role=\"img\" title=\"face vomiting\">:face_vomiting:</span></p>\n<p>Edit: Is \"disabling the global 'simp' lemma <code>ind_apply</code>\" worth a PR?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simps</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Representation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Coinvariants</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapDomainLinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rTensor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mul_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">map_one'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">map_mul'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IndV</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
